{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp","id":172633,"title":"Mechanical method of determining when Arcanoi Markings Deveolp?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-18T04:57:28-07:00","id":172633,"title":"Mechanical method of determining when Arcanoi Markings Deveolp?","content":"As written, a wraith acquires arcanos markings essentially when the ST, or perhaps the player, says so. This is kind of an important moment, since what markings your character has can have an effect on how people react to you... so I feel that it's important to have some sort of impartial system to describe when your character has acquired the markings of his arcanoi.<br /> <br /> A wraith can safely use his arcanoi a number of times equal to 5 + Appearance without worrying about gaining a marking.<br /> <br /> If a wraith goes without using that particular arcanoi for a week, have the ST roll the number of times used against difficulty 6. any successes are reduced from the number of times used. Failure or Botch means that the times used have not been reduced.<br /> <br /> After 5 + appearance uses, each time the wraith uses the arcanos roll appearance vs. difficulty 6. a success means that the wraith has avoided developing markings for his arcanos. A failure means that the wraith takes on the marking for the scene. A botch means that the wraith has gained the marking for that arcanos, permanently.<br /> <br /> Why Appearance? As this roll direclty affects a wraith's appearance, it seems appropriate, especially considering how a wraith's appearance often reflects their psychic self-image. These rolls represent a wraith's self-image resisting the corrupting influence of his arcanoi. Appearance tends to be an underused trait,<br /> <br /> This may be too complicated, and has the unfortunate downside of requiring the ST to keep track of how many times the PCs use arcanoi. If anyone else has a more elegant mechanical solution (Besides ST Fiat, though admittedly, that works too.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T08:48:44-07:00","id":172842,"title":"","content":"How about just tying it to the level in the Arcanoi? You learn more, you start showing the signs of it. No surpressing, repressing, etc. Lowest levels can be concealed,unless the Wraith (or Shadow, perhaps?) is really invested in the Arcanoi for some reason, then, lightly but more visibly. I'm with you on the marks being tied into the Wraith's Corpus vis-a-vis the interrelation with self-image. I doubt that one you get to 3 dots or above you CAN hide them anymore except by explicitly covering and concealing them in a manner that's pretty obvious.<br /> <br /> Ancillary question: Can you Moliate them away? If so, for how long? (Probably until you start using the Arcanoi again? Then they start 'fading&quot; back into view).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T12:28:04-07:00","id":173057,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp#post172633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, a wraith acquires arcanos markings\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not a bad mechanic. My troupe never did come up with a good system for developing Markings. I think we went with some sort of existentially role-played system. If the character began to see the Arcanoi as part of his identity, then Markings would develop. Basically, we made it player fiat rather than ST fiat. I<br /> <br /> On the matter of Arcanoi Markings (I apologize if I go slighty off-topic): What Arcanoi Markings would develop if a player made extensive use of Usury?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=172842#post172842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ancillary question: Can you Moliate them away? If so, for how long? (Probably until you start using the Arcanoi again? Then they start 'fading&quot; back into view).</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> I agree. I would have made a similar call. Do you think you could use Moliate to cover Moliate\u2019s Arcanoi Marking? (Which is what, btw? A porcelain-like Corpus?) </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T15:46:46-07:00","id":173274,"title":"","content":"I would always have markings show up at the 3rd dot of the Arcanoi. It was about the depth of understanding rather than the overall usage of the Arcanos in question that determined when they would appear. A wraith could have all the level one and two powers they wanted, and use them often without any chance of markings. Once that 3rd dot started to be developed, they would fade in. As to covering up, I'd let Moliate cover them for a scene before they start to fade back in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T00:44:44-07:00","id":173804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=172842#post172842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about just tying it to the level in the Arcanoi? You learn more, you start showing the signs of it. No surpressing, repressing, etc. Lowest levels can be concealed,unless the Wraith (or Shadow, perhaps?) is really invested in the Arcanoi for some reason, then, lightly but more visibly. I'm with you on the marks being tied into the Wraith's Corpus vis-a-vis the interrelation with self-image. I doubt that one you get to 3 dots or above you CAN hide them anymore except by explicitly covering and concealing them in a manner that's pretty obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a much simpler option... however you might have a character that likes to cause trouble with high levels of pandemonium but has been VERY careful not to use it enough to gain the marks... or the wraith that gets a lot of use out of a 1-dot power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=172842#post172842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancillary question: Can you Moliate them away? If so, for how long? (Probably until you start using the Arcanoi again? Then they start 'fading&quot; back into view).</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2nd edition book explicitly says that moliate cannot be used to remove arcanos markings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T02:56:55-07:00","id":173912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=173057#post173057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><br /> <br /> That\u2019s not a bad mechanic. My troupe never did come up with a good system for developing Markings. I think we went with some sort of existentially role-played system. If the character began to see the Arcanoi as part of his identity, then Markings would develop. Basically, we made it player fiat rather than ST fiat. I<br /> <br /> On the matter of Arcanoi Markings (I apologize if I go slighty off-topic): What Arcanoi Markings would develop if a player made extensive use of Usury?<br /> <br /> I agree. I would have made a similar call. Do you think you could use Moliate to cover Moliate\u2019s Arcanoi Marking? (Which is what, btw? A porcelain-like Corpus?) </span></div> </div> </div> </div>The markings are described in the last paragraph of the Guild section on each arcanoi. Some markings actually aren't markings at all, and instead manifest as quirks or mannerisms, or compel the wraith to carry certain objects or wear certain items of clothing... in the case of the latter two, it isn't clear whether these objects are part of the wraith's corpus or whether they seek out these items.<br /> <br /> In the case of Usury, the wraith tends to speak in precise, mathematical terms, and carries a set of scales to help balance the energy transferal. Masquers have a near-obsession with perfection, and their corpora are particularly malleable and look a bit too perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T06:48:30-07:00","id":174076,"title":"","content":"I was thinking I read in some book that they showed up with the third or fourth dot, but that could be completely wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1082-nfi","name":"NFI","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:40:37-07:00","id":174166,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=173912#post173912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Usury, the wraith tends to speak in precise, mathematical terms, and carries a set of scales to help balance the energy transferal. Masquers have a near-obsession with perfection, and their corpora are particularly malleable and look a bit too perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I\u2019m all too familiar with the nebulous (and borderline-nonexistent) Arcanoi Markings. Although we never came up with a mechanic for their development, my troupe did replace these \u201cmarkings\u201d with things a bit more\u2026discernable.<br /> <br /> Some examples:<br /> <br /> Usury: Vestigial talons form on the hands of the Wraith\u2019s Corpus. [RAW: they carry a set of scales?] <br /> <br /> Keening: The character\u2019s voice begins to sound like two or three people speaking in unison. [RAW: they carry a lute or something]<br /> <br /> Fatalism: When casually moving, Oracles sometimes appear to \u2018jump-cut\u2019 a few feet. {RAW: they like Tarot cards?]<br /> <br /> The idea was that after a short period of observation (say, a Scene, why not), you could have a good guess about the Arcanoi a Wraith is proficient with.<br /> <br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:54:05-07:00","id":174238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Old Rusty Pipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=173274#post173274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would always have markings show up at the 3rd dot of the Arcanoi. It was about the depth of understanding rather than the overall usage of the Arcanos in question that determined when they would appear. A wraith could have all the level one and two powers they wanted, and use them often without any chance of markings. Once that 3rd dot started to be developed, they would fade in. As to covering up, I'd let Moliate cover them for a scene before they start to fade back in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! That's really harsh... I like it! even though it is way less harsh than the rules apparently. But that rule seems to go too far. A lot of opportunities for disguise go right out the window if the marks bleed right through automatically. Want to know who the Masquer spy is? Look to see if your buddy has started looking like he's a mannequin made of shiny plastic....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-19-2014, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:59:13-07:00","id":174243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=173912#post173912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The markings are described in the last paragraph of the Guild section on each arcanoi. Some markings actually aren't markings at all, and instead manifest as quirks or mannerisms, or compel the wraith to carry certain objects or wear certain items of clothing... in the case of the latter two, it isn't clear whether these objects are part of the wraith's corpus or whether they seek out these items.<br /> <br /> In the case of Usury, the wraith tends to speak in precise, mathematical terms, and carries a set of scales to help balance the energy transferal. Masquers have a near-obsession with perfection, and their corpora are particularly malleable and look a bit too perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the Masquers one. But does anyone else hate the Usury marks as much as I do? There's got to be a better way than personality or apparel (which brings up what apparel is.... Corpus? Don't like that one so much. Moliated or soulforged wraiths? Most wraiths would be naked. Clothing as a mark of status. And, well, ick... Relics? I have done this one in the past and it worked. A lot of wraiths were bartering off their clothes as 0 dot Relics.... With some of the Moliated/soulforged stuff as status-symbols). Even equations etching themselves into their skin on their forearms, hands, face seems better, though a little derivative of other marks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:42:53-07:00","id":174273,"title":"","content":"I'll get the specific page numbers in a bit, since I don't have my books with me right now. I know that some of this comes from <i>Buried Secrets</i>. Arcanos marks fully manifest at the 3rd dot, though there might be some subtle lead-in, like a Harbinger whose eyes are milky white, cataract-like before turning all-black; or the Monitor who has an unblinking squint, like they're trying to block the sun from their eyes. The highest-level Arcanos is the most predominant when it comes to marks, with any other Arcanoi being more subtle in their leavings - for example, a Spook with Outrage 4 will have the knotted muscle look, but if they have Argos 3, they might also have one completely black eye, or maybe a hazy grey sheen over both eyes. Wraiths with Arcanoi of the same level fully get all appropriate marks.<br /> I believe the Guildbooks had expanded marks for some, notably the ones mentioned here. Chanteurs gained a sing-song-like quality to their voice that they could not cover; Usurers had a desiccated, gaunt look, or were grossly obese depending on if they were &quot;takers&quot; or &quot;givers.&quot;<br /> For Oracles, they have obscure, esoteric, and arcane symbols of fortune-telling etched (or burned, or however you want it) along their arms and forehead.<br /> Cheers!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:00:08-07:00","id":174282,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">For as much as I love (and played) Wraith, I never picked up any of the Guildbooks. I hope the GB-Marking-tweeks make it into Wr20. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:24:47-07:00","id":174559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=174166#post174166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><br /> Fatalism: When casually moving, Oracles sometimes appear to \u2018jump-cut\u2019 a few feet. {RAW: they like Tarot cards?]<br /> </span></div> </div> </div> </div>RAW is actually that they manifest &quot;arcane markings or symbols of Fate inscribed on their foreheads and arms. These sigils appear on their own and cannot be removed, and many appear to dance or move on their own&quot;. That they like Tarots, or other such props, is more of a matter of their preferred method of using their Arcanoi and this part of them and it's influence on their Arcanoi is handled more in their respective Guildbook, still the Sigils are the Arcanoi Markings and them using certain props is how they use their Arcanoi, some need more props than others.<br /> <br /> Also I find the Moliate's Malleable Corpus to be quite sufficient of an Arcanoi Marking even if it is not quite discernible by sight, which fit's well with a power that specifically sees most of it's use in disguise, but touch instead, Masquers Corpus feels softer in a slightly disturbing manner.<br /> <br /> Also I should admit that the Core book sometimes leaves a bit to be desired on the matter of Arcanoi Markings, like how it really does not emphasize the amount of crazy that Pandemonium inflicts upon it's users, but these are very nicely handled in the Guildbooks. I dare to suspect that the more indepth Arcanoi Markings of the Chanteurs is the obvious one, obsession with music and musical instruments or just slight whistling and humming when not paying attention to their own quirks, this easily leads to the situation where most who think of Chanteurs think about a Wraith with a musical instrument as described in the Core. But sadly we never got the rest of hte Guildbooks. Hopefully we get a new chance for those with the arrival of Wraith20.<br /> <br /> Similarly to my theory about the Chanteurs I do believe that the Usurer Markings are also more psychological in nature, starting to see everything around them in terms of energy transferals and becoming obsessed about precision and mathematics since to them everything is in the end simple numbers.<br /> <br /> Personally I do like the idea that some of these Markings are psychological in nature, like with the Puppeteers and Haunters yet can still manifest in their Corpus, since Corpus is the manifestation of the Wraith's mind in the end, like shown by the Flaw Aggravated Quirk for the Haunters and Sticky Corpus for the Puppeteers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T03:31:30-07:00","id":175116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/172633-mechanical-method-of-determining-when-arcanoi-markings-deveolp?p=174243#post174243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the Masquers one. But does anyone else hate the Usury marks as much as I do? There's got to be a better way than personality or apparel (which brings up what apparel is.... Corpus? Don't like that one so much. Moliated or soulforged wraiths? Most wraiths would be naked. Clothing as a mark of status. And, well, ick... Relics? I have done this one in the past and it worked. A lot of wraiths were bartering off their clothes as 0 dot Relics.... With some of the Moliated/soulforged stuff as status-symbols). Even equations etching themselves into their skin on their forearms, hands, face seems better, though a little derivative of other marks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always understood the clothing a wraith is... born... in is a part of the wraith's corpus and reflects the wraith's self-image. A biker may arrive in the shadowlands in jeans and a leather jacket, but can't take the jacket off, at least not without a masquers help. Or, optionally, the jacket itself might be a relic, in which case he could probably take it off, and might have other benefits as well (armor)<br /> <br /> I was looking at the Sandmen's book, and there is a section where it talks about their marking. They talk about how they gather dreamstuff (which they call gossamer) out of tradition, or for a particular fashion statement. The book notes that sandmen can cast aside their gossamer if they want, and without it there is no proof that a person is a sandman. Without the gossamer you might still be able to guess, though, because they tend to be flamboyant, extroverted or erudite. But the impression I get from the text is that they see this sort of thing as being a natural extension of being *actors*, not some mystical consequence of their arcanos. If someone pegs the Sandman for what he is, his likely reaction is going to be to take credit for their superior poise, their dramatic flair, while they rub their knuckles on their lapel.<br /> <br /> In the same way, I would expect usurers to feel the same way about their marking. They speak in numerical terms because to be a skilled Usurer takes a degree of precision. The scales are just useful. There may not be an in game benefit to the scales, but the character does... I mean, I can weigh two items with my hands and decide which is heavier, but I don't have to think about it so hard if I have a pair of scales to weigh with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}